87AFFF][/dim]plan:202609/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]agent_session_core_expand.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202609/agent_session_core_expand.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim] Parent: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202609/agent_session_rename.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-17m.2.1[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-17m/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]sase-17m.2.1.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Identity, launch, holds, and directive/editor surfaces[/bold #D7AFFF]        [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]identity-directives[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]identity-directives: rename agent_family.rs to agent_session.rs and the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]agent_identity, artifact_link, agent_launch, hold, editor, and LSP [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]family concept. Add the parse_agent_session_name and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]resolve_agent_session_parent bindings, accept %id session=, reserve [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]session/sessions, and flip editor completion to session= with companion [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sase tests that tolerate both core shapes.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Scan, runtime, lifecycle, runner, and stats wires[/bold #D7AFFF]             [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]scan-runtime[dim] · [dim][/dim]after identity-directives[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]scan-runtime: rename the family concept in agent_scan, agent_runtime, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]agent_clan_record, agent_cleanup, agent_ownership, agent_group_archive, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]agent_stats, runner_capacity, gate_followup, and their neighbours. Pin [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]legacy serde spellings, read new-then-legacy keys in hand-read JSON, and[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]add the reconcile_agent_artifact_index_dismissed_agent_session_members [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]binding.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Fleet core and gateway[/bold #D7AFFF]                                        [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]fleet[dim] · [dim][/dim]after scan-runtime[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]fleet: rename fleet_family.rs to fleet_agent_session.rs and the family [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]concept in fleet_*, fleet_contract, and sase_gateway. Add the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]fleet_followed_batch_agent_session_promotions binding, accept session: [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]logical-key segments and session-<hex> fallback ids on input, and keep [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]fleet_api_v1.json and emitted keys unchanged.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Classification sweep and cross-repo verification[/bold #D7AFFF]              [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]sweep[dim] · [dim][/dim]after fleet[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]sweep: classify every remaining famil hit in sase-core, fix stragglers, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]confirm byte-identical output and unchanged schema versions, and verify [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]that a sase workspace built against the final core passes sase tool run [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]check. Record follow-ups for wire-cutover and core-contract on the phase[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]bead.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-17m.2.1","llm_provider":"muse","model":"muse-spark-1.3-contributor","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-17m.2.1.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-47b9e3455338180449dc075559bc6546","started_at":"2026-09-24T02:56:43.889540+00:00","state":"completed"},{"capabilities":{"durably_revivable":true,"historically_viewable":true,"missing_requirements":[],"restartable":true},"commits":[],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"commits":{"digest":"a4e9dcff25d88322377cb581b