that already use [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]\"agent session\" for other things (provider transcripts, the ACE tmux [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]session, a single agent run, a workflow lifetime, fold scope), so the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]phrase is free for the new concept.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]sase-core additive rename[/bold #D7AFFF]                                     [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]core-expand[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-expand: non-breaking sase-core change. Rename the Rust internals to[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]agent-session vocabulary and add the new pyo3 binding names alongside [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the old ones. Inputs accept both old and new spellings; serialized [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]output stays byte-identical.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Python persistence and wire cutover[/bold #D7AFFF]                           [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]wire-cutover[dim] · [dim][/dim]after free-name, core-expand[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]wire-cutover: bump the core pin and switch sase to the new binding [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]names. Rename the Python wire mirrors and durable JSON fields: new data [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]is written only with agent_session keys, and readers accept both key [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]spellings. Rename the Agent model fields and the rebuildable caches.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Runtime, syntax, and CLI cutover[/bold #D7AFFF]                              [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]runtime-cutover[dim] · [dim][/dim]after wire-cutover[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]runtime-cutover: rename every non-ACE module and identifier. Make [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]session= / session: / --next-fork session / SASE_AGENT_SESSION_ATTACH [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]canonical and keep the old spellings working behind the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]legacy_agent_family_syntax sunset flag. Update CLI help and JSON output,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the editor bridge, and the skill templates.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]ACE agent session surfaces[/bold #D7AFFF]                                    [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]ace-cutover[dim] · [dim][/dim]after runtime-cutover[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]ace-cutover: rename ACE modules, row kinds, the grouping mode, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]visible copy (SESSION SHELLS, SESSION). Update keymap and help text, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]default_config.yml and the schema, perf baselines, and the PNG goldens, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]with no change to the performance contract.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Documentation and memory[/bold #D7AFFF]                                      [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]docs-memory[dim] · [dim][/dim]after runtime-cutover[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]docs-memory: rename docs/agent_families.md to docs/agent_sessions.md and[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]rewrite every concept mention in docs/ and the blog. Replace the Agent [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Family glossary strand with Sase Agent Session, update the related [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]strands and notes, then run sase memory init.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]sase-telegram cutover[/bold #D7AFFF]                                         [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]telegram[dim] · [dim][/dim]after runtime-cutover[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]telegram: move the /show session kind, formatting, help, docs, and tests[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]to the renamed sase APIs, and stop a missing import from silently [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]disabling the lookup.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]sase-core contract flip[/bold #D7AFFF]                                       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]core-contract[dim] · [dim][/dim]after ace-cutover, docs-memory, telegram[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-contract: breaking feat! sase-core change. Serialize the new key [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and value names, drop the legacy binding names, emit sessions/ link [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]paths and session: fleet keys, and bump the changed schema versions and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the fleet protocol. Keep aliases so legacy durable data still reads.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  9 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Pin bump and agents sidecar session pages[/bold #D7AFFF]                     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]session-pages[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core-contract[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]session-pages: bump the core pin and the Python schema mirrors. Publish [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]agents-sidecar pages under sessions/, keep permanent redirect stubs at [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the old families/ paths for historical commit-footer links, and update [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the sidecar docs, templates, and goldens.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  10 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Cross-repo audit, guardrail, and deploy[/bold #D7AFFF]                      [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]audit[dim] · [dim][/dim]after session-pages[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]audit: add a terminology regression test and sweep every repo, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]classifying each remaining \"family\" hit. Regenerate the chezmoi skill [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]copies from the landed tree and update the chezmoi ACE snippet.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-17m","llm_provider":"muse","model":"muse-spark-1.3-contributor","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__